WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.401
Welcome to Grade 6 English, Unit 6: People and Work.

2
00:00:03.481 --> 00:00:06.414
In this unit the focus is on people and work.

3
00:00:06.494 --> 00:00:12.239
You will explore the many different jobs and
professions that keep communities running,

4
00:00:12.319 --> 00:00:16.323
from physicians and lawyers to food vendors and commentators.

5
00:00:16.403 --> 00:00:21.880
You will learn how people choose their
careers, what skills different jobs require,

6
00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:28.240
and how the world of work connects to ideas of
fairness, justice, and community responsibility.

7
00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:33.864
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:33.944 --> 00:00:41.270
By the end of this unit, you will be able to identify
and describe a range of professions and career paths,

9
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.938
explaining the skills and training each one requires.

10
00:00:45.018 --> 00:00:50.752
You will also explain how personal interests
and strengths can guide career choices.

11
00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:58.781
You will also read a passage about careers and jobs and
answer comprehension questions at different thinking levels.

12
00:00:58.861 --> 00:01:01.342
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:01.422 --> 00:01:07.505
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: wisdom,
script, text, commentary, observation, caption.

14
00:01:07.585 --> 00:01:12.449
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

15
00:01:12.529 --> 00:01:16.293
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

16
00:01:16.373 --> 00:01:22.358
The reading sequence includes The People Who Keep
a Community Running and Four Professions, One Town.

17
00:01:22.438 --> 00:01:23.198
Read actively.

18
00:01:23.278 --> 00:01:27.342
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

19
00:01:27.422 --> 00:01:31.245
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

20
00:01:31.325 --> 00:01:36.310
The first language focus is Compound
Nouns: Closed, Hyphenated and Open Forms.

21
00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:42.090
A compound noun joins two or more words to
make one noun with a single, specific meaning,

22
00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:45.987
and English writes these compounds in three different forms.

23
00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:53.065
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

24
00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:57.408
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Career Interview Role-Play.

25
00:01:57.488 --> 00:02:01.565
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

26
00:02:01.645 --> 00:02:04.729
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

27
00:02:04.809 --> 00:02:08.017
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

28
00:02:08.097 --> 00:02:09.604
You are ready to begin.

29
00:02:09.684 --> 00:02:16.438
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

30
00:02:16.518 --> 00:02:19.751
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

31
00:02:19.831 --> 00:02:27.413
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
